backport: recover after Tc/Tw inside a TJ array (bug 709660)

BACKPORT of upstream mupdf 4a95c9651721091c86405e03965d2df52b2fe480, not a
change of ours. Drop it when the vendored mupdf moves past that commit - it is
on mupdf master but not in 1.28.2.

https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709660

Replaces our 0029-pdf-tj-array-tc-tw. Upstream adds the same break after
applying Tc/Tw inside a TJ array so a syntax error does not drop the rest of
the page. Covers #4157.
---
diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-interpret.c b/source/pdf/pdf-interpret.c
index cf4cf09..3864606 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-interpret.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-interpret.c
@@ -1595,6 +1595,7 @@ pdf_process_stream(fz_context *ctx, pdf_processor *proc, pdf_csi *csi, fz_stream
 									csi->stack[0] = pdf_to_real(ctx, o);
 									pdf_array_delete(ctx, csi->obj, n-1);
 									pdf_process_keyword(ctx, proc, csi, stm, buf->scratch);
+									break; /* keep parsing the rest of the array */
 								}
 							}
 						}
